When I try to open WSL it attemptsto pop openand closes right away
Alright Spencer — when WSL opens and immediately closes, that tells me something very specific:

Your WSL installation is broken at the bootstrap level, and Windows is trying to launch it but the subsystem crashes before it can display anything.

The good news is: this is fixable, and I can walk you through it cleanly.

Let’s go step‑by‑step and get your terminal stable so you can install the Solana CLI.

🔍 First: Confirm the exact failure
When WSL closes instantly, it usually means one of these:

WSL is installed but no Linux distro is installed

The distro is corrupted

The WSL kernel is missing or outdated

Virtualization is disabled

Windows features didn’t fully enable

We’ll fix all of these in order.

🛠️ STEP 1 — Check if WSL is actually installed
Open PowerShell (not WSL) and run:

Code
wsl --status
If it says something like:

“No installed distributions”

“Default distribution not found”

“WSL is not enabled”

…then we know exactly what’s wrong.

🛠️ STEP 2 — Install a Linux distro (most common fix)
If you never installed Ubuntu, WSL has nothing to open — so it closes instantly.

Run this in PowerShell:

Code
wsl --install -d Ubuntu
This forces Windows to install Ubuntu properly.

After installation, restart your PC.

Then try opening WSL again.

🛠️ STEP 3 — Reset the WSL kernel (second most common fix)
If the kernel is corrupted, run:

Code
wsl --update
Then:

Code
wsl --shutdown
Then try opening WSL again.

🛠️ STEP 4 — Make sure virtualization is enabled
WSL requires virtualization.

Check this:
Press Ctrl+Shift+Esc (Task Manager)

Go to Performance tab

Look for Virtualization: Enabled

If it says Disabled, you must enable it in BIOS.

🛠️ STEP 5 — Re-enable WSL features (if needed)
Run this in PowerShell as Administrator:

Code
dism.exe /online /enable-feature /featurename:Microsoft-Windows-Subsystem-Linux /all /norestart
dism.exe /online /enable-feature /featurename:VirtualMachinePlatform /all /norestart
Then restart your PC.

